  "currentRoundInspection": {
    "inspectedOn": "2026-10-16",
    "scope": "Two actually inspected whole oblique/elevated exterior pictures and standard viewer PMTiles/DEM only.No bespoke plans/surveys.No reference images redistributed or used as textures.",
    "pictures": [
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grazer_Dom_(1).jpg",
        "author": "Pedro J Pacheco",
        "date": "2014-08-22",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-3.0-AT",
        "observed": "Actually inspected full western/southern street oblique. Pale rendered Gothic hall,exposed stone buttresses,tall narrow pointed windows,large steep red tiled roof,west gable with round center window and tall side lights/decorated timber portal. Large green copper west roof lantern has dark glazed/louvred stage,broad cornices and curved onion roof/mini lantern/finial. Smaller eastern roof turret. Southern projecting Baroque chapel has pale pilasters,small round/octagonal upper lights,green hipped curved roof and central raised pediment/gold figure. Fresco artwork is not copied."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Graz_Dom_Schlossberg.jpg",
        "author": "Marion Schneider and Christoph Aistleiter",
        "date": "2009-10-25",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "observed": "Actually inspected elevated west roofscape. Broad continuous red tile nave gable,metal ridge/apron,large staged copper west lantern with bulb profile and small upper lantern,smaller east ridge turret. Separate green mausoleum dome and tower behind belong to the neighboring building and are excluded. Lower elevations partly occluded;no claim of exact hidden bays or present-day finish."
      }
    ]
